  "confidence": 0.9,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["T2", "R21"],
      "pins": ["T2.1", "R21.2", "R21.1", "M4.J1_12"],
      "nets": ["NET0057", "/NET0070"],
      "observed": "T2 gate (pin 1) is on net /NET0070, which connects through R21 to NET0057. NET0057 is the ESP32 IO2/SPI_MISO net, which the specification identifies as ATO_VALVE. Thus the main circulation-pump MOSFET T2 is driven by the ATO valve control signal.",
      "expected": "Per the specification, T2 is the main circulation-pump low-side switch and its gate should be driven from the ESP32 PUMP_MAIN signal (IO10) through R1/T1, not from ATO_VALVE (IO2).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"80\") (name \"NET0057\") ... (node (ref \"M4\") (pin \"J1_12\") (pinfunction \"IO2/SPI_MISO\") ...) (node (ref \"R21\") (pin \"1\") ...))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"52\") (name \"/NET0070\") ... (node (ref \"R21\") (pin \"2\") ...) (node (ref \"T2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"G\") ...))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T2 — IRLR2905 (DPAK N-MOSFET) | Main circulation-pump low-side switch | Netlist: drives PUMP_MAIN net to the 24 V main pump load; gate driven through R1 (100 Ω) from the ESP32 pin, pre-driven via T1 (BT3904 NPN level shifter)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The main circulation pump is controlled by the ATO valve signal instead of the intended PUMP_MAIN signal. This would cause the main pump to run when the ATO valve should open and likely prevent correct circulation-pump control, leading to incorrect hydroponic water flow and possible flooding or pump dry-run depending on the reciprocal ATO valve wiring.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a control-signal cross: the main circulation-pump MOSFET T2 gate is connected to the ATO_VALVE net (IO2) via R21 instead of the intended PUMP_MAIN net (IO10). This would make the main pump respond to the ATO valve control signal, a clear deviation from the specified design."
}

